Z||000026||filthyscarecrow||08-28-2001||12:26 AM||||any of you autoweek readers might remember a fabulous idea that some finnish company had a few years ago... (the whole thing was a joke, but the wheels started turning). it was called teh carpoon. like a harpoon, but for cars. the prusuing officer's car has one adn they just snag the offender and reel them in. fishing for perps, if you will... <P><BR>but then the editors took it too far... they told of a (fictitious) incedent where an officer speared a stillen GTZ supercharged, NOS suburban with 800+ Hp and the driver paniced and dragged the now helpless officer around town until he found a turn like #4 at indy and cracked the officers whip right off a cliff. or some such thing. <P>do i have a point? why yes! any solution anyone comes up with will never be successful 100% of the time. people are individuals, even if they all wear abercrombie and fitch, adn each will act and react differently. it's best to have a plan of action, but how often will the situation work out the way you plan? <BR>one writer's suggestion was to give the officers 911 turbo carrera 4's and send them to skippy barber's adn then let the games begin... if that's ever the case, i'll be the first one in line for "law enforcment 101."||||reg||1
